  "annotations": [
    { "id": "note-product", "page": "page-product", "x": 1560, "y": -150, "w": 420, "text": "Product · Direction C\n\nScreens with a dot in the header are clickable: Ship (change weight, package, extras, pick a rate, Buy), Shipments (filters), Batch (select rows), Billing (default card), Reports (date range, hover bars), Settings (tabs, label format), phone Ship flow (steps).\n\nAll names, addresses, rates and totals are sample data. Bracketed [placeholders] on the landing and tracking pages are real facts I don't have." },
    { "id": "note-system", "page": "page-system", "x": 0, "y": -130, "w": 420, "text": "System design · read 1 → 7\n\nArchitecture, then the data it stores, the API on top, and the three flows that carry money or state: buying a label, tracking, pay-as-you-go billing on Stripe. EasyPost is the single shipping provider — rates, labels, refunds, trackers, address verification — behind a thin interface (7), so nothing else in the system knows about it." },
    { "id": "note-dir-a", "page": "page-directions", "x": 0, "y": 900, "w": 320, "text": "A · Crisp utility\n\nFor: sellers shipping 20–200 packages a day who live in this screen. Numbers align, rows are dense, nothing decorative.\n\nTradeoff: reads cold to a first-time seller; the landing page has to do the warmth." },
    { "id": "note-dir-b", "page": "page-directions", "x": 1100, "y": 900, "w": 320, "text": "B · Warm & friendly\n\nFor: the kitchen-table seller shipping 3 a week who finds carrier sites scary. Copy talks, big targets, one card per rate.\n\nTradeoff: spends vertical space — batch shipping and dense lists need a tighter variant." },
    { "id": "note-dir-c", "page": "page-directions", "x": 2200, "y": 900, "w": 320, "text": "C · Bold editorial — chosen\n\nFor: a brand that wants to be remembered — the savings number IS the hero. Strong on marketing pages and the tracking page customers see.\n\nTradeoff: the hardest to keep readable in dense tables and settings screens; needs discipline." }
  ],
  "launch": { "view": "canvas", "page": "page-product" }
